Maintainer: Jeff Gardner <mailmasker-api01@forge.name>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), perl (>= 5.40)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/permittivity2/homelab

Package: homelab-postgres-exporter
Architecture: all
Depends: prometheus-postgres-exporter, sudo, openssl
Recommends: homelab-agent, homelab-node-exporter
Description: PostgreSQL metrics exporter wiring for the homelab-* ecosystem
 Wraps the Ubuntu-archive prometheus-postgres-exporter for the fleet DB
 host. On configure it bootstraps a read-only 'homelab_exporter' Postgres
 role (pg_monitor) using LOCAL sudo -u postgres -- never a stored network
 admin credential, same posture as homelab-database's bootstrap-app-role --
 writes the exporter's DATA_SOURCE_NAME, and advertises the exporter into
 the fleet topology (kind: metrics-exporter, :9187) so homelab-prometheus
 discovers and scrapes it. Install on the PostgreSQL host. The scrape
 firewall opening is handled fleet-wide by homelab-node-exporter.
